            <h3>Privacy Policy</h3>
            <p><strong>Effective August 14, 2025</strong></p>
            <p>CloudHost247 Isc ("we," "us" or "CloudHost247.com") cares about protecting the personal information of our customers and visitors who use our websites, products, or services (collectively, our "Users"). This privacy policy provides details about how your personal information is collected, shared, and used by us.</p>

            <h3>Information Covered by this Privacy Policy</h3>
            <p>This privacy policy covers personal information, including any information we collect, use, and share from you, as described further below. This privacy policy applies to all CloudHost247.com websites, our products and services, and our mobile applications (collectively, the "Services"). This privacy policy does not cover how our Users may use or share data that they collect using our Services.</p>
            <p>When you purchase a Service from us, your personal information will be collected, used, and shared consistent with this privacy policy as well as any product-specific addendums related to particular services offered by CloudHost247 Isc, which are incorporated into this privacy policy.</p>

            <h3>Information We Collect From You</h3>
            <p>In the course of your use of the Services, we obtain the following information about you, as described below. We collect this data for the purposes described under "How We Use Your Information."</p>

            <h3>1. Signing Up for Services; User Information</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Information you provide prior to any registration process, such as your email when you provide it to us.</li>
                <li>Information you provide during registration (such as your name, company name, email address, phone number, billing address or credit card information, geographic location, and industry), when you contact us (for support or otherwise), or when you use our products or services.</li>
                <li>Payment information you provide (via our Services or otherwise) when you purchase our products and services, including credit card data.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>2. Use of Services, Website Visits, and Support</h3>
            <p>We collect data related to your online activity with our Services, such as:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>IP address</li>
                <li>Browser type and version</li>
                <li>Geographic location</li>
                <li>Pages viewed</li>
                <li>Referral sources (how you got to our Services)</li>
                <li>Links you click to leave our Services</li>
                <li>Updates you make to your account</li>
                <li>Metadata about your use of our Services (clicks, opens, etc.)</li>
                <li>Interactions with videos or resources we provide</li>
                <li>Support requests and issue reports</li>
                <li>Device or other communication methods used</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We store this data in system log files, backend databases, and analytics systems.</p>
            <p>Your telephone conversations with us may be monitored or recorded.</p>

            <h3>3. Social Media</h3>
            <p>If you use your credentials from third-party social networking sites to log into some of our Services, we may receive information from those platforms (such as your name and email address to pre-populate forms). The specific information depends on your privacy settings with that social network.</p>

            <h3>4. Other Sources</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Information provided at events or seminars.</li>
                <li>Information from surveys.</li>
                <li>Publicly available information.</li>
                <li>Information you consent to share with us from third parties.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>How We Use Your Information</h3>
            <p>We use your personal information to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Provide the requested Services.</li>
                <li>Ensure the proper functioning of our Services.</li>
                <li>Offer and improve our Services.</li>
                <li>Provide technical support.</li>
                <li>Facilitate navigation and usability of our Services.</li>
                <li>Conduct advertising and marketing (with your consent where required).</li>
                <li>Advertise third-party products/services (with your consent where required).</li>
                <li>Diagnose technical issues.</li>
                <li>Maintain security and compliance.</li>
                <li>Administer our websites.</li>
                <li>Personalize your experience.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We also use aggregated and anonymized data for reporting trends and statistics. Payment details are used only to process transactions. Recorded calls may be used for quality control and training.</p>

            <h3>Sharing of Information</h3>
            <p>We may share your personal information:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>With Partners to help you use our services, provide offers, or deliver relevant products (with your consent where required).</li>
                <li>With Third-Party Vendors to assist with customer service, fraud prevention, analytics, advertising, hosting, and other operational needs.</li>
                <li>For Corporate Transactions in the event of mergers, acquisitions, or sales of assets.</li>
                <li>With Authorized Users such as account sub-users you grant access to.</li>
                <li>For Legal Reasons where required by law, court order, or to prevent harm.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We will never sell your credit card or sensitive payment information.</p>

            <h3>Security</h3>
            <p>While we take appropriate technical and organizational measures (including TLS encryption for financial data), no transmission over the Internet, email, or text can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>

            <h3>Tracking Technologies and Cookies</h3>
            <p>We use cookies, web beacons, and similar tools for analytics, advertising, and service functionality. See our Cookie Policy for details and opt-out options.</p>

            <h3>Choice/Opt-out</h3>
            <p>You can:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Opt-out of marketing emails via the unsubscribe link or by emailing privacy@cloudhost247.com.</li>
                <li>Contact us to opt-out of marketing phone calls.</li>
                <li>Manage cookies via your browser or our Cookie Policy.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Retention of Personal Information</h3>
            <p>We retain your information for as long as necessary to provide services, meet legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce agreements up to seven years after account closure, unless otherwise required by law.</p>

            <h3>You're Rights (GDPR)</h3>
            <p>Where GDPR applies, you have rights to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Access: know what data we hold and how it's used.</li>
                <li>Portability: receive certain data in a portable format.</li>
                <li>Correction: fix inaccurate/incomplete data.</li>
                <li>Erasure: request deletion under certain conditions.</li>
                <li>Restriction: limit processing under certain conditions.</li>
                <li>Objection: stop certain processing, including marketing.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Requests require identity verification and may be refused if legally justified.</p>

            <h3>Children</h3>
            <p>Our Services are not intended for those under 18, and we do not knowingly collect data from minors.</p>

            <h3>Data Transfer</h3>
            <p>Your data may be processed or stored in the United States or other countries outside your location, with safeguards to ensure compliance with privacy laws.</p>

            <h3>Notification of Changes</h3>
            <p>We may update this Privacy Policy and will notify you via our website or email before significant changes take effect. Continued use of our Services after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>

            <h3>Contact Us</h3>
